      "hints": [
        "Set $-6(3-2x)^2 + 24 = 0$ to get $(3-2x)^2 = 4$.",
        "Solve for $x = \\frac{1}{2}$ and $x = \\frac{5}{2}$.",
        "Substitute both $x$ values into $y$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0$ to find the stationary points:\n$$-6(3 - 2x)^2 + 24 = 0 \\implies (3 - 2x)^2 = 4$$",
        "Solve for $x$ by taking square roots:\n$$3 - 2x = 2 \\implies 2x = 1 \\implies x = \\frac{1}{2}$$\n$$3 - 2x = -2 \\implies 2x = 5 \\implies x = \\frac{5}{2}$$",
        "Evaluate $y$ when $x = \\frac{1}{2}$:\n$$y = \\left(3 - 2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)^3 + 24\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = 2^3 + 12 = 20 \\implies \\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 20\\right)$$",
        "Evaluate $y$ when $x = \\frac{5}{2}$:\n$$y = \\left(3 - 2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)\\right)^3 + 24\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right) = (-2)^3 + 60 = 52 \\implies \\left(\\frac{5}{2}, 52\\right)$$"
      ],
